    <statement><p>Find an interval of t-values such that <m>c(t) = (\cos{t}, \sin{t})</m> traces the upper half of the unit circle (in the counter-clockwise direction).</p>
<p>interval = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Note: Use lowercase "pi" for <m>\pi</m>.</p>
<p>Example answer: <m>\left[0,1\right]</m>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left[0,3.14159\right]</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>t = 0</m>, we have <m>c(\pi) = (1, 0)</m>.  As t increases from <m>0</m> to <m>\pi</m>, the x-coordinate of <m>c(t)</m> decreases from 1 to -1, and the y-coordinate increases from 0 to 1 (at <m>t = \frac{\pi}{2}</m>) and then returns to 0.  Thus, for t in <m>[0,3.14159]</m>, the equation traces the upper part of the circle.


</solution>
